  "summary": "Heuristic partitions and feature calls in transcriptomics are being replaced by tests with error control and explicit null models.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is formal statistical inference applied to structures that are usually produced heuristically. Two items test partitions directly: SigDoTS applies hypothesis testing with FWER control to candidate spatial transcriptomics domains, merging or retaining them through null simulations, and ProClust assesses scRNA-seq cluster significance by merging overclustered groups using log-concave cluster modelling and projection-based testing. IsoVita extends this to compositional features that vary along continuous covariates, using change point and spline tests for isoform usage. RoDPAA addresses multi-view microbiome integration with a dissimilarity-based principal angle framework that avoids log-ratio transforms. What is new across these items is that each decision is paired with an explicit null model or error criterion.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
